ui-fab-tokens-are-organized-by-size-and-color-values-below-follow-the-native-component-defaul = FAB tokens are organized by size and color. Values below follow the native component defaults used on this page.

ui-40dp-small-56dp-80dp-medium-96dp-large = 40dp small · 56dp · 80dp medium · 96dp large

ui-12dp-16dp-20dp-28dp-corners = 12dp · 16dp · 20dp · 28dp corners

ui-icon-color-at-8-hover-and-10-focus-or-press = Icon color at 8% hover and 10% focus or press

ui-keep-the-state-layer-color-equal-to-the-icon-color-when-a-non-default-color-mapping-is-use = Keep the state layer color equal to the icon color when a non-default color mapping is used, so feedback stays visible on every tone.

ui-a-fab-is-a-single-container-with-one-icon-it-has-no-visible-label-the-icon-carries-the-mea = A FAB is a single container with one icon. It has no visible label; the icon carries the meaning and the accessibility label names the action.

ui-2-icon = 2  Icon

ui-one-container-one-icon-one-action = One container, one icon, one action.

ui-container-tones-map-to-the-primary-secondary-and-tertiary-color-roles-either-as-containers-3175 = Container tones map to the primary, secondary, and tertiary color roles, either as containers or as solid accents. Each tone pairs with its matching on-color for the icon.

ui-surface-color-styles-are-still-available-but-no-longer-recommended-prefer-a-container-tone = Surface color styles are still available but no longer recommended; prefer a container tone so the action reads as primary.

ui-states-communicate-elevation-and-interaction-a-fab-rests-at-level-3-rises-to-level-4-on-ho = States communicate elevation and interaction. A FAB rests at level 3, rises to level 4 on hover, keeps level 3 while focused or pressed, and sharpens its state layer as interaction increases.

ui-accent = Accent

ui-height-icon-size-and-corner-radius-scale-together-reserve-16dp-margins-around-a-floating-a = Height, icon size, and corner radius scale together. Reserve 16dp margins around a floating action, and keep a 48dp minimum interactive target for the smaller sizes.

ui-padding-around-icon = Padding around icon

ui-container-sizes-of-the-small-regular-medium-and-large-fabs = Container sizes of the small, regular, medium, and large FABs.

ui-icon-to-container = Icon to container

ui-baseline-fab-token-sets-are-still-published-but-the-surface-color-styles-are-no-longer-rec = Baseline FAB token sets are still published, but the surface color styles are no longer recommended in the expressive update. Prefer the primary container mapping shown on this page.

ui-baseline-value = Baseline value

ui-16dp-corners = 16dp corners

ui-both-baseline-and-expressive-mappings-keep-the-same-interaction-model-elevation-level-3-at = Both baseline and expressive mappings keep the same interaction model: elevation level 3 at rest, level 4 on hover, and a state layer that matches the icon color.

ui-use-one-fab-for-the-most-common-or-important-action-on-a-screen-keep-the-icon-clear-and-un = Use one FAB for the most common or important action on a screen. Keep the icon clear and understandable, and avoid covering content that people need while the action is visible.

ui-do-one-fab-with-a-familiar-icon-for-the-primary-action = Do: one FAB with a familiar icon for the primary action.

ui-don-t-two-fabs-competing-for-equally-important-actions = Don't: two FABs competing for equally important actions.

ui-a-fab-represents-one-action-not-a-collection-of-actions = A FAB represents one action, not a collection of actions.

ui-do-not-use-a-fab-for-destructive-or-dismissive-actions = Do not use a FAB for destructive or dismissive actions

ui-keep-the-icon-understandable-without-extra-explanation = Keep the icon understandable without extra explanation

ui-prefer-a-fab-menu-when-several-related-actions-belong-together = Prefer a FAB menu when several related actions belong together

ui-a-fab-performs-its-action-immediately-when-several-related-actions-belong-together-use-a-f = A FAB performs its action immediately. When several related actions belong together, use a FAB menu, and when the action needs a visible label, use an extended FAB instead.

ui-use-when = Use when

ui-one-primary-action-with-a-universally-understood-icon = One primary action with a universally understood icon

ui-extended-fab = Extended FAB

ui-the-action-needs-a-visible-text-label = The action needs a visible text label

ui-two-to-six-related-actions-belong-to-one-trigger = Two to six related actions belong to one trigger

ui-the-fab-is-a-single-container-with-a-centered-icon-keep-the-icon-simple-and-recognizable-a = The FAB is a single container with a centered icon. Keep the icon simple and recognizable, and place the accessible label on the container rather than on the icon.

ui-default-to-the-primary-container-tone-secondary-and-tertiary-tones-separate-a-floating-act = Default to the primary container tone. Secondary and tertiary tones separate a floating action from other primary-colored elements, while solid accent tones raise its emphasis.

ui-place-a-fab-at-the-bottom-end-of-the-screen-above-the-bottom-navigation-bar-or-any-bottom = Place a FAB at the bottom end of the screen, above the bottom navigation bar or any bottom sheet. Keep a 16dp margin from the screen edges and from other floating elements.

ui-fabs-should-have-margins-of-16dp-and-must-not-cover-the-navigation-bar = FABs should have margins of 16dp and must not cover the navigation bar.

ui-choose-the-size-by-window-class-the-small-and-regular-fabs-suit-compact-layouts-while-the = Choose the size by window class. The small and regular FABs suit compact layouts, while the medium and large sizes give the action more presence in expanded layouts.

ui-the-same-action-at-two-size-presets = The same action at two size presets.

ui-a-fab-can-hide-while-content-scrolls-down-and-reappear-when-scrolling-up-so-it-never-block = A FAB can hide while content scrolls down and reappear when scrolling up, so it never blocks the content people are reading. Keep it reachable and avoid animating it on every frame.

ui-hide-or-show-the-floating-action = Hide or show the floating action

ui-hide-fab = Hide FAB

ui-show-fab = Show FAB

ui-fab-hidden-while-scrolling = FAB hidden while scrolling

ui-hiding-is-a-scroll-behavior-not-a-state-change-the-action-keeps-its-position-and-its-acces = Hiding is a scroll behavior, not a state change: the action keeps its position and its accessible name when it returns.

ui-navigate-to-and-activate-the-fab = Navigate to and activate the FAB

ui-identify-the-action-from-its-accessible-label = Identify the action from its accessible label

ui-the-fab-exposes-one-action-named-by-its-accessibility-label-activating-it-increments-the-c = The FAB exposes one action named by its accessibility label; activating it increments the counter.

ui-the-fab-is-a-large-target-the-smallest-container-is-40dp-and-the-interactive-target-never = The FAB is a large target: the smallest container is 40dp and the interactive target never drops below 48 × 48dp. Keep the icon contrast at 3:1 or higher against the container.

ui-above-three-to-one-add = Above three to one: add

ui-below-three-to-one-add = Below three to one: add

ui-a-fab-is-a-single-focus-stop-focus-is-drawn-as-a-ring-around-the-container-and-it-should-f = A FAB is a single focus stop. Focus is drawn as a ring around the container, and it should follow the reading order of the screen rather than jumping to the corner first.

ui-press-tab-to-reach-the-action-the-container-receives-focus-once = Press Tab to reach the action; the container receives focus once.

ui-keep-the-fab-clear-of-navigation-bars-sheets-and-snackbars-it-should-stay-in-the-same-corn = Keep the FAB clear of navigation bars, sheets, and snackbars. It should stay in the same corner across screens, so people can find it without searching.

ui-navigate-to-the-fab = Navigate to the FAB

ui-activate-the-fab = Activate the FAB

ui-the-fab-behaves-like-a-button-for-keyboard-input-one-focus-stop-activated-by-space-or-ente = The FAB behaves like a button for keyboard input: one focus stop, activated by Space or Enter, with a focus ring around the container rather than around the icon.

ui-a-fab-has-no-visible-label-so-its-accessibility-label-must-name-the-action-do-not-describe = A FAB has no visible label, so its accessibility label must name the action. Do not describe the icon; describe what activating it does.

ui-do-add-button-the-label-names-the-action = Do: “Add, button” — the label names the action.

ui-don-t-plus-icon-describing-the-glyph-does-not-explain-the-action = Don't: “Plus icon” — describing the glyph does not explain the action.

ui-keep-the-same-label-when-the-fab-hides-and-returns-and-provide-a-tooltip-only-as-a-visual = Keep the same label when the FAB hides and returns, and provide a tooltip only as a visual hint — the accessible name stays on the container.
